WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:16.020
Good morning Hank, it's Monday, January 8th.
Sarah and I are about to drive out of Asheville,

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.520
on our way to Birmingham, Alabama.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.020
I know you're gonna be here soon, but in the
meantime I thought you should enjoy how pretty

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:27.530
it is. We're going down the dirt road on the
way to the other dirt road that leads away

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:31.609
from Mom's house. And Dad's house! Sorry Dad,
geez.

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:35.780
I would like to congratulate you on successfully
completing the Strawberry Hill challenge,

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.830
except that you didn't complete it! Drinking
Sutter Home wine when you've been challenged

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.820
to drink Strawberry Hill is like slow dancing
with Teddy Ruxpin when you've been challenged

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.640
to wrestle a grizzly bear. Sutter Home may
be terrible, but at least it's derived from

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.640
grapes.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.480
Strawberry Hill isn't made out of grapes.
It's made out of strawberries. Just kidding,

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:58.100
it's made out of apple wine, malt, red dye,
and the fires of hell.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.239
Hank, as you know, I had surgery on my mouth
a few weeks ago. After they sewed my gum back

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:07.730
into my mouth, my mouth tasted like cement
and blood and burnt meat. And you know how

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:14.920
after any dental procedure they make you drink
that, like, green, gross, minty alcoholy stuff

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.799
and then spit? Strawberry Hill tast-

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:21.600
*achoo* (whispers) That was the Yeti!

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.890
Strawberry Hill tastes exactly like that spit.
Do you think I'm funny? Am I trying too hard?

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:32.420
When? The whole time? Teddy Ruxpin? It's just
you get that way around the camera.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.420
So Hank, today is a very significant day,
and I'll tell you why. It's January 8th and

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:42.100
the first draft of my new novel is due on
January 21st. Now, I'm not a mathematician,

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.539
but I know a couple, so I called Daniel Biss
and he told me that January 21st is only 13

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.749
days away.

00:01:47.749 --> 00:01:52.170
Aside from the problem of actually finishing
the book, which is, admittedly, a pretty serious

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.170
problem, there's the problem that it doesn't
have a title. I would feel a lot better if

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:01.530
I actually had a title for the novel so that
I could say, you know, in ten days I have

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:08.920
to turn in the first draft of my new novel,
The Babysitter's Club 26: Claudia's Sad Goodbye.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:13.700
I've been thinking of using either Shakespeare
or the Bible. You've got a lot of great Shakespearean

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:20.120
titles over the years, like: Infinite Jest,
The Dogs of War, Brave New World, In Cold

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.709
Blood. And there are also a lot of great Bible
titles like: East of Eden, Song of Solomon,

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:30.690
or Rich Dad Poor Dad. Of course in the Biblical
version of Rich Dad Poor Dad, rich dad gets

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:35.760
turned into a pillar of salt and, uh, poor
dad is exalted above all others. Anyway Hank,

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.200
I'm hopeful you'll be able to come up with
a title for me.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:44.120
Project idea: the Brotherhood 2.0 Book Club.
I'll read a book you suggest if you read a

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:49.760
book I suggest. My first suggestion? Either
"What is the What," by Dave Eggers or "We

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.400
Wish to Inform You That Tomorrow We Will be
Killed With Our Families," by Philip Gourevitch.

